{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, thanks. I’ve been having this abdominal pain again—same kind as my old pancreatitis episodes. It started about a week ago with nausea, then the pain came back in the middle and right side, going through to my back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Was it as severe as your last pancreatitis episode?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not quite as bad, but still pretty uncomfortable. I had a CT scan six days ago—my doctor said there might be some inflammation in the tail of my pancreas."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I reviewed that. It showed a slightly bulky tail but no clear signs of active pancreatitis. We’ll need to look deeper. You mentioned you left the hospital yesterday after getting orange juice and vomiting—why did you come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just wasn’t getting better. The nausea kept coming back, and I felt weak. I knew I needed more help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That was the right call. We’re going to keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—for now, give you IV fluids, and control your pain and nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Will I be able to eat soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start slow. Once your symptoms settle, we’ll try clear liquids. It might take a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ve also been feeling a bit feverish—temperature up to 100."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We saw that. Your urine test showed some signs of infection—moderate bacteria and white cells—so we started you on Levaquin for a UTI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I’ve had UTIs before. I’ve also been having trouble emptying my bladder sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be contributing. We’ll treat the infection and monitor. We also checked your blood work—your hemoglobin has been dropping a bit, so we’re watching for anemia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had iron deficiency before. Is that related to the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Given your history of malabsorption and Sjogren’s, we’re concerned there might be an issue in your small intestine. We’re planning an EGD and capsule endoscopy to look inside."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What’s a capsule endoscopy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You swallow a small pill-sized camera that takes pictures as it moves through your gut. It helps us see the small bowel, which we can’t reach with regular scopes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds interesting. When will that happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Early next week. First, we need you stable and hydrated. We also did an ultrasound today to check your gallbladder—everything looked normal, so it’s not gallstones causing this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2149-09-20 15:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. My mom had her gallbladder out—always worried I’d get it too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2149-09-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2149-09-21 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. Nausea is less, but I still have some pain in the upper right side."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2149-09-21 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning show your kidney function is good, and your amylase and lipase are normal—so no active pancreatitis. But your potassium is a bit low at 3.1, so we’re giving you some supplements."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2149-09-21 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had low potassium before—especially when I was on full-dose Florinef. I’m on half now, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2149-09-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we kept it at half-dose because of that. Your blood pressure has been on the lower side—around 95 systolic—so we held your Betaxolol for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2149-09-21 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t felt dizzy, but I know I’d get more tachycardic if I stood up for long."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2149-09-21 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep monitoring. For now, we’re going to try advancing your diet to clear liquids if you’re up for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2149-09-21 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. I’m tired of just IV fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2149-09-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well with clear liquids yesterday. Today, we’re giving you toast. How’s your stomach holding up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2149-09-22 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. I had the whole piece and no vomiting. Pain is still there but milder."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2149-09-22 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re switching your pain meds from IV to oral Dilaudid. You can take it every few hours as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2149-09-22 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I’d rather not be on IVs anymore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2149-09-23 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today we did your EGD and capsule endoscopy. The upper endoscopy didn’t show anything obvious, but we took biopsies from your duodenum."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2149-09-23 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What did they find?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2149-09-23 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The biopsies show chronic duodenitis—ongoing inflammation. It could be from celiac disease, Crohn’s, or another form of IBD. We’re sending more tests to figure it out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2149-09-23 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a sigmoidoscopy years ago that showed inflammation. Could this be Crohn’s?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2149-09-23 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible. That’s why we tried to do a colonoscopy—to look at the rest of your colon. But even after your prep, there was still too much stool."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2149-09-23 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I thought I cleared out. What happens now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2149-09-23 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll need to come back and do a two-day GoLytely prep to clean things out fully. Then we can get a clear view."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2149-09-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. You’ve been on solids, no vomiting, pain is much better. We’re thinking about discharge in a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2149-09-24 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What will I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2149-09-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue advancing your diet slowly. Stay on the omeprazole we started—it helps with gut inflammation. And take the Creon with meals; it helps with digestion since you have malabsorption."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2149-09-24 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve taken Creon before. How long should I stay on it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2149-09-24 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For now, indefinitely. We’ll reassess once we get all your biopsy results and complete the colonoscopy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2149-09-25 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your UTI treatment is complete—three days of Levaquin. No more fevers, and your symptoms have improved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2149-09-25 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better. My bladder feels normal now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2149-09-26 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re clearing you for discharge today. You’re tolerating food, pain is minimal, and you don’t need IV meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2149-09-26 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2149-09-26 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll need to schedule the colonoscopy with a full prep. We’re also adding Midodrine for your orthostatic symptoms, and we lowered your Betaxolol dose to 10mg to keep your heart rate stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2149-09-26 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2149-09-26 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue amitriptyline for sleep, Lexapro for mood, and Florinef at 0.2mg twice daily. Take the hydromorphone only if pain flares up, and don’t hesitate to come back if you can’t keep liquids down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2149-09-26 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I’m glad I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2149-09-26 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did the right thing. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2149-09-20 14:46:00",
    "admission_end": "2149-09-26 20:19:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for recurrent abdominal pain similar to prior pancreatitis episodes, but with normal lipase levels and only mild CT findings. She was managed with NPO status, IV fluids, and pain control, then gradually advanced to a solid diet. A UTI was treated with a 3-day course of levofloxacin. EGD and capsule endoscopy revealed chronic duodenitis, suggesting possible small bowel disease or IBD, though the etiology remained unclear. A colonoscopy was attempted but unsuccessful due to inadequate bowel prep, requiring a future repeat with full GoLytely preparation. Her orthostatic hypotension was managed with dose adjustments to fludrocortisone and betaxolol, and she was discharged home in good condition, tolerating oral intake and requiring no IV medications.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute pancreatitis",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Unspecified intestinal malabsorption",
      "Von Willebrand's disease",
      "Sicca syndrome"
    ]
  }
}
